# Build output
build/bin/
build/cache/
build/stage-*/
dist/

# Frontend
node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Runtime work directories (sidecar output)
geosense-run-*/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
.temp
# Grown canopy meshes. The app always writes these into a temp work dir;
# one lands here only when the sidecar action is run by hand without one.
sidecar/*.glb

# Agent permissions, which belong to a workstation rather than to the project.
# Only the local file: .claude/ itself stays available for whatever the project
# chooses to share, which is the split the harness assumes between the two.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Experiments. The scripts are versioned because they are the argument; what
# they fetch and what they render at archival size is not, because git keeps
# every byte forever and all of it regenerates by running them again.
experiments/data
# Rendered output, all of it regenerable and one TIFF of it 39 MB. The two
# figures that need a public URL are copied into docs/img/spectral instead, so
# nothing here is the only copy of anything.
experiments/figures
# Downloaded third-party material: the ESA response functions and an EcoSIS
# package. Committing them would also redistribute someone else's data.
experiments/s2_srf.xlsx
experiments/ecosis_soybean.csv
docs/user-manual/scripts
docs/user-manual/png-images
docs/user-manual/capas
docs/user-manual/guides

# The screenshot masters, kept on disk and out of the history.
#
# They are 3824 px PNGs with the window's alpha, ~35 MB for four, and the README
# ships 1800 px WebP derived from them at 521 KB. Committing the masters would
# put that weight in every clone forever, and deleting them is worse: the JPEGs
# in 7509678 lost the alpha channel because the masters had already been thrown
# away, and there was nothing left to re-encode from.
docs/img/*/original/
